<article class="env-lemma" id="08ZF">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08ZF">Lemma <span data-tag="08ZF">5.3.2</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a continuous map of topological spaces. If $Y$ is Hausdorff, then the graph of $f$ is closed in $X \times Y$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The graph is the inverse image of the diagonal under the map $X \times Y \to Y \times Y$. Thus the lemma follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/08ZE" data-tag="08ZE">5.3.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>